main() {
    static float a[] = {13, 24, 1.5, 4.5, 5.4, 3.5};
    float *j, *k;
    j = a;
    k = a + 4;
    j = j * 2;
    k = k / 2;
    printf("%f %f", *j, *k);
}

explanation:
A = {4n + 2} = {6, 10, 14, 18, 22, ...}
B = {3n} = {3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18, ...}

A ∩ B = {6, 18, 30, 42, ...}

This can be written as {12n - 6 | n is a natural number}

Check: n=1 → 6, n=2 → 18, n=3 → 30, n=4 → 42 ✓

Therefore, the correct answer is (d) {12n - 6 | n is a natural number}.
